# This repository is developed on Linux and every text file is stored with LF.
#
# Without this file, Git for Windows' default (core.autocrlf=true) rewrites the
# working tree to CRLF on checkout. That is invisible while you stay on Windows,
# because Python's text mode writes CRLF too, so `make vectors` still compares
# equal. It breaks the moment the same checkout is built under WSL or Linux:
# vectors.py then writes LF while claude/cc700-test-vectors.md on disk has CRLF,
# every one of the 472 lines differs, and `make test` fails on its first step.
# Shell scripts checked out with CRLF also fail with "bad interpreter".
#
# Normalise to LF in the repository and in the working tree on every platform.
* text=auto eol=lf

# Windows batch files are the exception: cmd.exe can mis-parse a .bat checked out
# with LF. gradlew.bat is already stored with CRLF, so leave it untouched rather
# than renormalising it; -text means Git never converts it in either direction.
*.bat -text
*.cmd -text

# Files Git must never line-ending-convert or diff as text.
*.png binary
*.jpg binary
*.bin binary
*.fit binary
*.zip binary
*.apk binary
*.ttf binary
*.woff2 binary
